1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:05,139
9 hours, 47 minutes at your desk.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,178
So where did the day go?

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,645
You remember the standup. Lunch. A bug fix, maybe.

4
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:15,600
The rest is a blur of tabs, chats, and quick checks.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,706
Then Friday, someone asks for your hours.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,300
Meet Cadence.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:25,473
It remembers your day, so you don't have to.

8
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:30,580
It notes the app or site in front of you, and gives you back the whole day.

9
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:36,406
Every 15 seconds. Quietly. Automatically.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,164
Minutes become your day. Your week. Your year.

11
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:46,642
Start a focus session, and Cadence keeps distractions out.

12
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,119
Every session gets a focus score.

13
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,750
Reports by project and client.

14
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:55,376
And Friday's timesheet? Already done.

15
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,927
No account. No cloud. No analytics.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,186
Your data stays on your Mac.

17
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:06,207
9:47. Now you know where it went.

18
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,329
Cadence. Free, for your Mac.
